I have everything I need. I verified the real code at every site and found one material correction to the LOCATION FINDINGS. Here is the plan.

---

# Implementation plan: variable snippet depth (full enclosing-function body for top-K search hits)

## Key correction to the location findings (read first)

The findings claim "the CLI text case needs NO change and agent has no budget." **Half wrong.** `runSearch` captures `contextBudget := flags.MaxContextBytes` (16 KB) at cli/search.go:58 **before** zeroing `flags.MaxContextBytes` for agent at :61-63, then passes that captured budget into `writeAgentSearch(..., contextBudget)` at :133. The agent path re-applies it through `fitAgentSearchResults` → `rankedAgentSearchBudgets` (already front-weighted; rank-1 gets ~1.4 KB at 16 KB/20 results) → `agentSearchBlock`, which **re-truncates** the snippet to that per-result budget. So a full body emitted by the sem layer is silently shrunk back for `--format agent` — the exact format the swebench agent uses to make its def/grep decisions.

Therefore the change is **two coordinated edits**:
- **Edit A (sem/search.go)** — produce the full body + protect it from the JSON byte budget. Fully delivers `text`/`json`/`ndjson`, and is the precondition for agent.
- **Edit B (cli/search.go)** — reserve enough of the agent wire budget for the top-K so `agentSearchBlock` doesn't re-truncate. **Required for `--format agent`.** Without it the win never reaches the agent.

